Host-side gtest unit tests for crosspoint-reader.

Build and run:

  cmake -S test -B build/test
  cmake --build build/test
  ctest --test-dir build/test --output-on-failure -j

Run a single suite directly:

  cmake --build build/test --target StreamingJsonParserTest
  build/test/streaming_json_parser/StreamingJsonParserTest --gtest_filter='*'

Google Test is fetched via CMake FetchContent on first configure; the pinned
version lives in test/CMakeLists.txt.

Some directories are not CMake suites: ble_hid_decoder, ble_key_binding,
crosspoint_state, json_conversions, kosync_messages, opds_servers and
recent_books hold
a make_corpus.py that writes a golden corpus for a Rust crate's tests (see the
script's docstring); kosync_messages, crosspoint_state and recent_books also
have a check_shim.sh, which runs the corpus's steps through the C++ shim over Rust.
json_oracle holds what they share (oracle.py: the JSON value generator, the
build over C++ from git, --check; check_shim.sh: the build over a shim;
driver_util.h and stubs/: the drivers' hex helpers and host stubs).
